<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37700" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-lĭgo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To bind on before</i>, <i>to
			bind</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arida sarmenta praeligantur cornibus boum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cauda pecoris quam arctissime praeligata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					29, 2, 10, § 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salice marginem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					17, 14, 24, § 109</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To bind around</i>, <i>tie about</i>
			a thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">statuae coronam candida fascia praeligatam
					imponere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars palmitis praeligata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 22, 35, § 180</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linum, quo praeligata infra caput vipera
					pependerit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					30, 5, 12, § 40</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<i>To bind up</i>, <i>tie up</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">os praeligatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Inv. 2, 50, 149</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnera nodo Herculis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 6, 17, § 63</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>To cover</i>, <i>veil</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestibus capita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 102, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to bind</i>, <i>fetter</i>, <i>charm</i>: o
			praeligatum pectus! <i>bound up</i>, i. e. <i>obdurate</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Bacch. 1, 2, 28</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
